$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 1634-04-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Borylation of
2-Alkylpyridine Derivatives (Table 2, Entry 1). In a glove box,
Silica-SMAP (0.070 mmol/g, 85.7 mg, 0.0060 mmol, 2.0 mol%),
bis(pinacolato)diboron (2) (76.2 mg, 0.30 mmol), and anhydrous, degassed
hexane (1.0 mL) were placed in a 10 mL glass tube containing a magnetic
stirring bar. A solution of [Ir(OMe)(cod)]2 (2.0 mg, 0.0030 mmol, 1.0
mol%) in hexane (2.0 mL) and 2-isopropylpyridine (1b) (109.0 mg, 0.9
mmol) were added successively. The tube was sealed with a screw cap and
removed from the glove box. The reaction mixture was stirred at 60 °C for
12 h, and filtered through a glass pipet equipped with a cotton filter.
Solvent was removed under reduced pressure. An internal standard
(1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane) was added to the residue. The yield of the
product 3b was determined by 1H NMR (109%). The crude material was then
purified by Kugelrohr distillation, to give the corresponding product
3b(52.0 mg, 0.22 mmol in 73% isolated yield). 3e, Colorless oil, NMR
yield (%)b 106(79); 3e' (C4 and C5 borylation), NMR yield (%)b 11
2-[2-(4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pentyl]pyridine (3e):
1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 0.88 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 1.12-1.18 (m, 2H), 1.23 (s,
6H), 1.24 (s, 6H), 1.29-1.40 (m, 2H), 1.42-1.55 (m, 1H), 2.82 (dd, J =
16.2, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 3.07 (dd, J = 16.2, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 7.22 (t, J = 5.7 Hz,
1H), 7.28 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.71 (td, J = 7.4, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 8.55 (d, J
= 7.1 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.26, 22.24, 25.49 (2C), 25.60 (2C),
33.27, 38.09, 80.87 (2C), 121.66, 123.48, 138.44, 144.86, 162.72. A
signal for the carbon directly attached to the boron atom was not
observed. HRMS–ESI (m/z): [M+H]+ Calcd for C16H27O2N10B, 275.21657;
found, 275.21659.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, solid-supported catalyst, catalyst on silica gel
(ligand), arylboronates obtained in 11% yield, silica-SMAP used as
catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Primary and Secondary Alkylboronates through Site-Selective
C(sp3)-H Activation with Silica-Supported Monophosphine-Ir Catalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kawamorita, Soichiro; Murakami, Ryo; Iwai, Tomohiro; Sawamura, Masaya
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(8), 2947-2950

